    "imagery": {
      "word": "IMAGERY",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "The work of one who makes images or visible representation of objects; imitation work; images in general, or in mass. \"Painted imagery.\" Shak. In those oratories might you see Rich carvings, portraitures, and imagery. Dryden.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Fig.: Unreal show; imitation; appearance. What can thy imagery of sorrow mean Prior.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The work of the imagination or fancy; false ideas; imaginary phantasms. The imagery of a melancholic fancy. Atterbury.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rhetorical decoration in writing or speaking; vivid descriptions presenting or suggesting images of sensible objects; figures in discourse. I wish there may be in this poem any instance of good imagery. Dryden.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
