    "imaginary": {
      "word": "IMAGINARY",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Existing only in imagination or fancy; not real; fancied; visionary; ideal. Wilt thou add to all the griefs I suffer Imaginary ills and fancied tortures Addison. Imaginary calculus See under Calculus. which involves the impossible operation of taking the square root of a negative quantity; as, sq. root-9, a + b sq. root-1. surfaces, etc., imagined to exist, although by reason of certain changes of a figure they have in fact ceased to have a real existence. illusive.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "An imaginary expression or quantity.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
